  whatwrong="In `routes/signatories.ts` the catch of the nominate route `POST /api/signatories` first reads `error.code === '23505'` (a unique-violation answers 409 CONFLICT) and then logs `Failed to nominate signatory` with `error: String(error)` and answers the constant 500. If the thrown value is a revoked Proxy, the property read `error.code` itself throws a TypeError inside the catch; if it is an Error whose `message` getter throws, `String(error)` throws. Either way the catch throws before it can answer: the async handler rejects and, under Express 4, the request gets NO RESPONSE (gate 104, G104-F3). **Both reads MUST be fixed together:** guarding only `String(error)` would still hang on a revoked Proxy at `error.code`."+ctxtail,
  callers="CALLERS: the route is mounted by `index.ts` at `/api/signatories` and called by HTTP clients only. The handler's single write is `INSERT INTO signatories` (an authorised-signatory nomination); the catch runs AFTER that statement was issued or rejected and persists nothing itself. WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the sites): an Error without a readable `code` (or with any code other than 23505) is logged with `String(error)` and answered with the constant 500 `INTERNAL_ERROR` / `Failed to nominate signatory`; an Error with code 23505 is answered 409 CONFLICT and not logged. After the fix an unreadable thrown value gets exactly the first of those: the constant 500, one `logger.error` line with the constant reason `unreadable thrown value`; the cells assert the status, the body, the logged context and that the database stand-in was called once. Today (unreadable): the request gets NO answer and nothing is logged. Persisted state: identical to an ordinary Error in every position (the catch persists nothing); the INSERT is the same single statement in all cases. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state:** for an unreadable thrown value only, the nominate route answers its constant 500 and logs a constant reason instead of never answering; an unreadable `code` is treated as no code (so never 409). Recommended tier 1 (authorised-signatory authority route; Kam's tier-1-with-Opus-gate ruling).",
