  callers="CALLERS: the routes are mounted by `index.ts` at `/api/third-party-verifiers` and called by HTTP clients only. Register issues `INSERT INTO third_party_verifiers` (status `pending`); approve issues `UPDATE third_party_verifiers SET status = 'active', api_key_hash = ...` (the one-time API key is generated BEFORE the write and shown only in the success response). The catches run after those statements were issued or rejected and persist nothing themselves. WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the sites): an Error without a readable `code` (or any code other than 23505) is logged with `String(error)` and answered with the constant 500 (`Failed to register verifier` / `Failed to approve verifier`); register with code 23505 answers 409 CONFLICT. After the fix an unreadable thrown value gets exactly the constant 500 with one `logger.error` line carrying the constant reason `unreadable thrown value`; the cells assert status, body, logged context and that the database stand-in was called once. Today (unreadable): NO ANSWER and nothing logged. Persisted state: identical to an ordinary Error in every position (the catch persists nothing). As gate 104 noted (G104-F3), a throw AFTER the approve UPDATE loses the one-time API key for an ordinary Error too: pre-existing and unchanged. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state:** for an unreadable thrown value only, the register and approve routes answer their constant 500 and log a constant reason instead of never answering; an unreadable `code` is treated as no code (never 409). Recommended tier 1 (third-party verifier authority routes: registration and API-key issuance; Kam's tier-1-with-Opus-gate ruling).",
